# No Duplication

Before implementing any new logic, search first:

1. `src/lib/money.ts` – pricing, rounding, currency formatting, cart totals
2. `src/lib/quantityFormat.ts` – all unit/quantity labels (Kit, Vial, Packung)
3. `src/lib/shop/shopAreaPricing.ts` – area-specific price calculation
4. `src/lib/shop/shopAreas.ts` – area types, constants, profile helpers
5. `src/lib/shop/priceLabels.ts` – price column label copy
6. `src/lib/shop/display.ts` – product name normalisation, grouping, sorting
7. `src/lib/shop/cartDisplay.ts` – cart line display (names, quantity labels, subtitles)
8. `src/lib/constants.ts` – `QUERY_KEYS`, app constants, bucket names
9. `src/services/` – existing Supabase calls (may be extendable)
10. `src/hooks/` – existing TanStack Query hooks
11. `supabase/migrations/` – existing SQL functions and RPCs

## Specific SSoT functions – never reimplement

| What you need | Use |
|---|---|
| Effective unit price (normal vs. bulk) | `getEffectiveUnitPrice` in `money.ts` |
| Apply role markup | `applyRoleMarkup` in `money.ts` |
| Area catalog unit | `shopAreaCatalogUnit` in `shopAreaPricing.ts` |
| Full area+role sell price | `shopAreaSellUnitPriceForProductRole` in `shopAreaPricing.ts` |
| Area pricing profile | `pricingProfileForArea` in `shopAreas.ts` |
| Area from URL | `shopAreaFromPath` in `shopAreas.ts` |
| Sale mode (kit vs vial noun) | `saleModeForShopArea` in `shopAreas.ts` |
| Quantity label (any context) | `formatProductQuantity` in `quantityFormat.ts` |
| Cart line totals | `calculateCartTotals` in `money.ts` |
| Order charges | `summarizeOrderCharges` in `money.ts` |
| Query cache key | `QUERY_KEYS.xxx` in `constants.ts` |

## When extending is better than creating

- A new shop area feature: extend `shopAreaPricing.ts` or `shopAreas.ts`, not a new file.
- A new admin area config type: add to the existing `AdminShopAreas.tsx` tab system, not a new page.
- A new quantity noun context: extend `quantityFormat.ts`, not an inline string.
- A new RPC: check if an existing one can be parameterised first.

## Scope of changes

Only change files directly needed for the task. Do not refactor, rename, or reformat unrelated code in the same PR.
